cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository — the results, the data artifacts, or the protocol — please cite it as below."
title: "Synthetic Players: pre-registered, mechanically adjudicated experiments on LLM game play"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nakajima
    given-names: Yohei
repository-code: "https://github.com/yoheinakajima/synthetic-players"
license: MIT
version: phase4-final
date-released: "2026-07-28"
abstract: >-
  A research program on how large language models play games, run under
  sealed pre-registration with fail-closed mechanical adjudication and
  byte-exact replay from an append-only event store. Central finding:
  subject behavior is driven by local semantic-textual content, not payoffs
  and not display mechanics; the cross-vendor twin inverts per channel.
  Data artifacts (event store, ledgers, adjudication records) are released
  under CC BY 4.0 as versioned release assets.
keywords:
  - game theory
  - large language models
  - preregistration
  - reproducibility
  - mechanical adjudication
